OL,3,GNEWSAMuck-spreading: The smellier the
OL,4,Abetter as farmers ask for patience
OL,5,
OL,6,FFarmers are asking people to be patient
OL,7,Fwith the smell of manure as they spread
OL,8,Fit on their fields to prepare the land
OL,9,Ffor next year's crops.
OL,11,FMuck-spreading is the process of
OL,12,Fdistributing animal manure across
OL,13,Ffarmland as a natural fertiliser and
OL,14,Ftypically takes place twice a year, in
OL,15,Fspring and late summer.
OL,17,FAlthough "it might smell a bit",
OL,18,Faccording to farmer Ben Clappison, from
OL,19,FCowlam, East Yorkshire, he says it is
OL,20,Fimportant as it helps improve the land
OL,21,Fand reduces the amount of chemical
OL,22,Ffertilisers.
OL,23,APub: 26-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,384,380,200,160,0,100
